Kludge Options
How to modify the source code to achieve various mesh results

1. Convert 3D anisotropic model to 3D isotropic model
In src/meshfem3D/model_aniso_mantle_cij.f90.
At line 623, toggle if-statement (true = isotropic; false = anisotropic)
Default = true (isotropic)!

2. Convert 3D model to 1D model
In src/meshfem3D/model_aniso_mantle_cij.f90.
At lines 321-322, set interpolation points (tet, ph) to some value outside the 3D model domain e.g., (0.d0, 0.d0)
Note, the 1D values depend on the option used for oneD_flag defined below
Default = 3D interpolation!

3. Extrapolation schemes
In src/meshfem3D/model_aniso_mantle_cij.f90.
Controlled by the definition of oneD_flag at line 309
oneD_flag = 0: Extrapolate to 1D isotropic average *OR* far-field model
+ At line 890, reset 1D average profile to far-field
oneD_flag = 1: Extrapolate to reference 1D profile (defined in src/shared/get_model_parameters.F90, line 474)
oneD_flag = 2: Extrapolate to nearest boundary (lateral extension of model)
Default oneD_flag = 0 and far-field!

4. Remove Crust
In meshfem3D_models.F90.
At lines 700, define suppress_mantle_extension = .false. to interpolate values above Moho.
Default = Not activated; 1D uniform crust added

5. Modified AK135 Moho and Crustal Velocities
In src/shared/get_model_parameters.F90
At line 474, 'REFERENCE_1D_MODEL' defines the default 1D model for the 3D geodynamic models
+ We are using AK135 (REFERENCE_MODEL_AK135F_NO_MUD)
+ We are using 1-element crust (ONE_CRUST = .true.)
At line 1316, you can change the depths of discontinuities used in creating the mesh
+ I shifted Moho to 14.3 km depth with and mid-crust to 7.0 km
In src/meshfem3D/model_ak135.f90 update the radius sampling and desired velocities
+ I used uniform crustal properties (rho = 2.82; vp = 6.15; vs = 3.655; Qk = 1170; Qm = 502)
**This is a better way to accomplish 4 if you do not want to interpolate model to surface but still want uniform iso crustal layer

